load @term/seed/code/machine/turing
  find turing-machine

# Computability: the study of what can be computed at all, independent of speed. A function is computable if some Turing
# machine produces its output for every input, and the computable functions are exactly the same whether defined by
# Turing machines, the lambda calculus, or recursive functions, the robustness that is the Church-Turing thesis. Some
# precise questions are NOT computable, the halting problem chief among them: no machine decides, for every program and
# input, whether the program halts. The form carries the Turing machine the computability is measured against.
form computability
  link machine, like turing-machine
